{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgQ6Dy9kzpZy29Yj5zWQ6", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The file is a Linux x86_64 build, but your machine runs Windows 11. It won't run natively in PowerShell, so you'll need WSL (Windows Subsystem for Linux) to install it. First, find the file.\n\n**Step 1: Find the tarball (PowerShell)**\n\nThis searches your user profile, which covers Downloads, Desktop and Documents:\n\n```powershell\nGet-ChildItem -Path $env:USERPROFILE -Filter \"dataforge-1.4.0-linux-x86_64.tar.gz\" -Recurse -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object FullName, Length, LastWriteTime\n```\n\nIf nothing shows up, it may be on another drive, or the name may have changed (for example `dataforge-1.4.0-linux-x86_64 (1).tar.gz`). Try a wildcard search instead: change `-Filter` to `\"dataforge*\"` and run it against `C:\\` or the other drive.\n\n**Step 2: Install (once you have the path)**\n\n1. Check that WSL is available by running `wsl --list --verbose`. If no distribution is listed, run `wsl --install` from an admin PowerShell, reboot, and then continue.\n2. Copy the tarball into WSL and extract it into a new, empty directory. Don't extract it into a folder that already has other files. Windows drives are visible in WSL under `/mnt/c/...`.\n3. Open the extracted folder's `README` or `INSTALL` file and follow it. Read any `install.sh` before running it, since it came from a download.\n4. If the vendor publishes a checksum, compare it against `sha256sum` of the tarball before installing.\n\nSend me the path the search finds, or tell me if it finds nothing. If you tell me which WSL distro you have, I can write the exact extract and install commands.\n\n```result\n{\"outcome\": \"recommendation\", \"commands\": [\"Get-ChildItem -Path $env:USERPROFILE -Filter \\\"dataforge-1.4.0-linux-x86_64.tar.gz\\\" -Recurse -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object FullName, Length, LastWriteTime\"], \"environment_facts\": [{\"fact\": \"User's OS is Windows 11 Education, with PowerShell as the primary shell\", \"source\": \"observed\"}, {\"fact\": \"User profile appears to be C:\\\\Users\\\\user\", \"source\": \"observed\"}, {\"fact\": \"The file is a Linux x86_64 tarball and cannot run natively on Windows\", \"source\": \"user\"}, {\"fact\": \"WSL may not be installed or configured\", \"source\": \"assumed\"}, {\"fact\": \"The tarball is somewhere under the user's profile folder\", \"source\": \"assumed\"}], \"question\": null}\n```"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1169, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1169}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "283c6a1d-15dc-48b7-9cf2-c7b93f2fd9c8", "uuid": "e3440aac-70de-4b1c-b6a9-b2a3c2ddd905", "timestamp": "2026-10-26T02:52:12.491Z", "request_id": "req_011CgQ6DxsdYQqsiPeEXV2Ga"}
